      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Planning a concrete project starts with understanding the costs. Our Concrete Price Calculator helps you estimate the total expense for ready mix concrete pricing based on project dimensions, concrete type, and local pricing. Whether you are budgeting for a new driveway, patio, or foundation, accurate cost estimation prevents budget overruns and financial surprises.

The cost of concrete depends on several factors: volume (cubic yards), concrete type (standard, high-strength, stamped), delivery distance, and local labor rates. Standard ready-mix concrete costs $120–$150 per cubic yard, while bagged concrete runs approximately $4–$6 per 80lb bag. A typical 10×10 foot slab at 4 inches thick requires about 1.23 cubic yards — costing roughly $150–$185 for ready-mix or $50–$60 for bagged concrete (plus your labor).

Beyond the concrete itself, a complete project budget should include: gravel base material ($15–$20 per cubic yard), rebar or wire mesh reinforcement ($0.15–$0.30 per square foot), form lumber ($2–$4 per linear foot), and finishing tools. Labor costs for professional installation range from $4–$8 per square foot depending on complexity and region.

Our Concrete Price Calculator focuses on the concrete volume and bag estimation, which is the core material cost driver. By entering your exact dimensions, you get a precise volume calculation that you can multiply by your local per-yard or per-bag pricing. The built-in 5%% waste buffer ensures your estimate covers real-world conditions like spillage and form irregularities.

Use this tool alongside our Square Footage Calculator and Gravel Calculator to plan your complete construction project from start to finish.',
