The density of standard concrete is approximately 150 pounds per cubic foot (2,400 kg/m³). This means a typical 4-inch thick, 10×10 foot slab requires about 1.23 cubic yards of concrete — or roughly 56 bags of 80lb Quikrete mix. Understanding these numbers helps you plan delivery logistics, labor scheduling, and budget allocation. Whether you need a sidewalk and walkway projects estimate for a small backyard project or a commercial foundation, accurate calculation is the foundation of every successful pour.

Our tool supports imperial and metric units, multiple bag sizes (40lb, 60lb, 80lb, 25kg, 40kg), and provides instant results with no signup required. Use the related tools below to plan your full construction project — from square footage to gravel base calculations.',
