      'article' => 'Plan your concrete wall project accurately with our Concrete Wall Calculator. Whether you are building a retaining wall, a foundation wall, or a boundary barrier, retaining and boundary wall projects requires precise volume calculations that account for wall height, length, and thickness.

Poured concrete walls offer superior strength compared to block construction — a standard 8-inch poured wall delivers approximately 3,000 PSI compressive strength versus 1,500 PSI for standard CMU. For basement walls, retaining walls, and structural applications, poured concrete is often the preferred choice.

A typical residential foundation wall is 8–10 inches thick and 8 feet tall. A 100-linear-foot perimeter at 8 inches thick and 8 feet tall requires approximately 19.75 cubic yards of concrete. That is two full truckloads of ready-mix. Our Concrete Wall Calculator computes this instantly based on your input dimensions.

Retaining walls have unique design considerations: they must resist lateral earth pressure, water pressure, and surcharge loads. Wall thickness, reinforcement spacing, and footing dimensions all depend on the retained soil height. For walls over 4 feet, professional engineering design is typically required.

Our free calculator provides accurate volume estimates for any wall configuration. Use it alongside our Rebar Calculator (coming soon) and Square Footage Calculator for complete project planning.',
