      'article' => 'Calculate the concrete needed for pier and column volume estimation with our Concrete Pier Calculator. Cylindrical piers, columns, and post holes require different math than rectangular slabs — volume is calculated using π × radius² × height. Our tool simplifies this by converting standard length × width inputs into precise volume estimates.

A typical deck pier is 12 inches in diameter and 48 inches deep, requiring approximately 0.65 cubic feet of concrete — about 1.5 bags of 60lb mix per pier. A 12×12 deck might need 9–12 piers, totaling 6–8 cubic feet. Our Concrete Pier Calculator handles these calculations automatically.

Fence post holes are typically 8–10 inches in diameter and 24–36 inches deep. Each hole requires about 0.25–0.50 cubic feet of concrete, meaning a single 60lb bag can fill 1–2 post holes. For a 100-foot fence with posts every 8 feet, you will need approximately 13 posts and 7–13 bags of concrete.

