      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Our Concrete Cubic Yard Calculator helps you determine exactly how many cubic yards of concrete to order for cubic yard computation for ordering. Cubic yards are the standard unit used by ready-mix concrete suppliers across North America, and ordering the right amount is critical — too little means a mid-pour shortage, too much means wasted material and money.

One cubic yard of concrete equals 27 cubic feet and covers approximately 81 square feet at 4 inches thick, or 54 square feet at 6 inches thick. These numbers are essential for planning driveways, patios, sidewalks, and foundation slabs. Our calculator converts your length, width, and depth measurements directly into cubic yards with a built-in 5%% waste buffer.

Ready-mix concrete is typically delivered in trucks that carry 8–10 cubic yards per load. For residential projects, many suppliers offer short-load deliveries of 1–3 yards, though short-load fees may apply. Knowing your exact yardage helps you optimize delivery logistics and avoid both over-ordering and costly second trips. Use our Concrete Cubic Yard Calculator to get the precise number before calling your supplier.

The cost of ready-mix concrete varies by region but typically ranges from $120–$150 per cubic yard for standard 3,000 PSI mix. Specialty mixes (high-strength, fiber-reinforced, colored) cost more. By accurately calculating your yardage, you can get precise cost quotes and avoid budget surprises. Our tool supports both imperial and metric measurements for international users.

Professional contractors rely on accurate yardage calculations for every pour. Whether you are building a commercial foundation or a backyard patio, our free online Concrete Cubic Yard Calculator gives you the precision you need in seconds.',
