      ),
      'article' => 'Need to know exactly how many bags of concrete to buy? Our Bags of Concrete Calculator takes the guesswork out of how many 60lb or 80lb bags needed. Simply enter your project dimensions — length, width, and thickness — and instantly see how many 40lb, 60lb, or 80lb bags you need to complete the job without waste or shortage.

Bagged concrete is the go-to choice for small to medium projects: fence posts, mailbox bases, small slabs, repair patches, and stepping stones. Each bag size yields a different volume of mixed concrete: a 40lb bag yields approximately 0.30 cubic feet, a 60lb bag yields 0.45 cubic feet, and an 80lb bag yields 0.60 cubic feet. Our calculator uses these industry-standard yield values to give you an accurate bag count.

One of the biggest challenges in how many 60lb or 80lb bags needed is understanding the relationship between area, depth, and volume. For example, a 4×4 foot area at 4 inches deep requires about 5.33 cubic feet of concrete — that is 12 bags of 60lb mix or 9 bags of 80lb mix. These numbers add up quickly for larger projects, which is why professional-grade estimation matters. Our tool also includes a 5%% waste buffer so you are never caught short on pour day.

Whether you are using Quikrete, Sakrete, or another brand, the yield per bag is consistent within standard tolerances. For very large projects (over 1 cubic yard), consider ordering ready-mix concrete by the truck — it is more cost-effective and ensures a continuous pour. Our Bags of Concrete Calculator helps you make that decision by showing both bag count and total cubic yardage side by side.

All calculations happen instantly in your browser — no registration, no downloads, no hidden costs. Your dimensions stay private and are never stored on our servers.',
