      ),
      'article' => 'Our Concrete Calculator Metric provides metric system concrete estimation using meters and centimeters. This tool is designed for international users and projects using the metric system, converting dimensions into cubic meters and metric bag quantities.

In the metric system, concrete volume is measured in cubic meters (m³). One cubic meter equals approximately 1.31 cubic yards or 35.31 cubic feet. Standard metric concrete bags come in 25kg and 40kg sizes, yielding approximately 0.015 m³ and 0.024 m³ respectively.

A typical metric slab calculation: 3m × 3m × 0.10m = 0.90 m³. With a 5%% waste buffer, this becomes 0.945 m³ — requiring approximately 63 bags of 25kg mix or 40 bags of 40kg mix. Our calculator handles this conversion automatically.

