Most colleges require a minimum 2.0 GPA for graduation and good standing. Dean\'s List typically requires 3.5 or higher. Graduate school admissions generally expect 3.0+ for master\'s programs and 3.3+ for doctoral programs. Professional schools (medical, law, dental) often have even higher thresholds. Understanding where you stand each semester helps you make informed decisions about course loads, study strategies, and academic goals.

