          'a' => 'Many high schools assign equal credit to all courses, making non-credit GPA identical to credit-weighted GPA. Some assign different credits for half-year vs. full-year courses.',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I find my course credit hours?',
          'a' => 'Check your course catalog, registration portal, or academic transcript. Standard college courses are 3-4 credits. Labs are often 1 credit. Seminars vary from 1-3 credits.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What if my courses have different credit weights?',
          'a' => 'For the most accurate GPA, enter actual credit hours. Our calculator multiplies each grade by its credits to properly weight higher-credit courses.',
