      'tool_slug' => 'gpa-calculator',
      'h1' => 'Law School GPA Calculator',
      'title' => 'Law School GPA Calculator - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free Law School GPA Calculator to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Law school admissions are intensely GPA-focused, and our Law School GPA Calculator helps you understand law school admission GPA requirements. The Law School Admission Council (LSAC) calculates a standardized GPA for every applicant that may differ from your university transcript GPA. Understanding how LSAC computes your GPA is essential for realistic law school targeting.

LSAC recalculates your GPA using all undergraduate grades, including courses you may have retaken. While your university may replace the original grade with the retake grade, LSAC includes both. LSAC also converts all grades to a standard 4.0 scale, which can change your GPA if your school uses a different system. These recalculations mean your LSAC GPA may be higher or lower than your transcript GPA.

Law school admissions rely heavily on two numbers: LSAC GPA and LSAT score. Top 14 law schools (T14) typically admit students with 3.7+ GPAs and 170+ LSAT scores. Top 50 schools generally expect 3.4+ GPAs. However, a strong LSAT score can partially compensate for a lower GPA, and vice versa. Understanding your competitive position requires knowing your exact GPA on the LSAC scale.

Use our calculator to estimate your GPA using the standard 4.0 scale. Enter all courses from your undergraduate career, including any repeated courses. This gives you a close approximation of what LSAC will calculate when processing your application.',
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How does LSAC calculate GPA?',
          'a' => 'LSAC recalculates your GPA using all undergraduate grades on a standard 4.0 scale, including both original and retake grades for repeated courses.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does LSAC include graduate school grades?',
          'a' => 'No, LSAC GPA includes only undergraduate coursework. Graduate and professional school grades are reported separately.',
        ),
