          'q' => 'What GPA do I need for law school?',
          'a' => 'Top 14 schools: 3.7+, Top 50: 3.4+, Most accredited schools: 3.0+. GPA is considered alongside LSAT scores for a holistic evaluation.',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can a high LSAT compensate for low GPA?',
          'a' => 'Partially yes. A strong LSAT score can offset a lower GPA, though both factors matter. Score "splitters" with high LSAT and lower GPA can still gain admission to competitive schools.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does LSAC use plus/minus grades?',
          'a' => 'Yes, LSAC uses the full plus/minus scale (A, A-, B+, B, etc.) when your transcript reports them. Flat letter grades are converted at their base value.',
        ),
      ),
