      'title' => 'GPA Calculator from Grades - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free GPA Calculator from Grades to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Converting between different grading systems is essential for academic planning, and our GPA Calculator from Grades simplifies converting letter grades to GPA. Whether you need to convert letter grades to GPA values, translate percentage scores to the 4.0 scale, or compare international grading systems, accurate conversion ensures you understand your academic standing.

The standard US conversion scale maps letter grades to GPA points: A+ = 4.0, A = 4.0, A- = 3.7, B+ = 3.3, B = 3.0, B- = 2.7, C+ = 2.3, C = 2.0, C- = 1.7, D+ = 1.3, D = 1.0, F = 0.0. For percentage-to-GPA conversion, common thresholds are: 93-100%% = 4.0 (A), 90-92%% = 3.7 (A-), 87-89%% = 3.3 (B+), 83-86%% = 3.0 (B), and so on. Note that conversion scales can vary by institution.

International students often need to convert their home-country grades to the US 4.0 scale. Indian percentage systems (typically 0-100), UK classification systems (First, 2:1, 2:2, Third), and European ECTS grades all require different conversion formulas. While no single conversion is universally accepted, our tool provides the standard US scale that most American colleges use as a baseline.

Enter your grades in letter format into our calculator and it will automatically apply the correct GPA point values. For percentage-based conversion, divide your grades into letter equivalents first, then use our calculator for the GPA computation. This gives you an accurate 4.0-scale GPA that you can compare across institutions.',
