    'gpa-calculator-without-credits' => 
    array (
      'tool_slug' => 'gpa-calculator',
      'h1' => 'GPA Calculator Without Credits',
      'title' => 'GPA Calculator Without Credits - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free GPA Calculator Without Credits to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Not all GPA calculations require credit hours, and our GPA Calculator Without Credits handles GPA estimation without credit hours with ease. Some academic programs, high schools, and informal tracking scenarios do not use credit-weighted systems. In these cases, GPA is simply the average of grade point values across all courses, treating each course equally.

Without credit weighting, GPA calculation is straightforward: sum all grade point values and divide by the number of courses. For example, if you earn grades of A (4.0), B+ (3.3), A- (3.7), B (3.0), and A (4.0) across five courses, your unweighted-by-credits GPA is (4.0 + 3.3 + 3.7 + 3.0 + 4.0) / 5 = 3.60. This method gives equal weight to every course regardless of contact hours or difficulty.

Many high schools use this equal-weight approach because courses typically carry the same number of credits per semester. Middle schools and junior high schools almost universally use non-credit-weighted GPA. Even in college settings, a simplified calculation can be useful for quick estimates when you do not have credit information readily available.

Our calculator supports both credit-weighted and simplified GPA calculations. For non-credit modes, enter 1 as the credit value for all courses to get an equal-weight average. This gives you a straightforward grade point average that treats every course identically.',
      'faq' => 
