      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'University students need reliable tools for academic planning, and our WIU GPA Calculations provides accurate results for Western Illinois University GPA tool. Every university uses GPA as a key metric for academic standing, scholarship eligibility, honors programs, and graduation requirements. Our calculator uses the standard 4.0 grading scale adopted by virtually all American universities.

University grading policies can vary significantly. Some institutions use plus/minus grading (A, A-, B+, B, B-, etc.) while others use flat letter grades (A, B, C, D, F). Some award A+ grades that count as 4.0, while others give them 4.3. Our calculator supports the full 4.0 scale with plus/minus grades, adhering to the most common system used nationwide.

Academic policies regarding GPA vary by university: minimum GPA for graduation (typically 2.0), Dean\'s List threshold (typically 3.5+), academic probation trigger (typically below 2.0), and eligibility for honors programs (typically 3.3+). Many universities also calculate a major GPA (courses within your declared major) separately from your cumulative GPA. Understanding both numbers is important for academic planning.

Our free online calculator helps you track your semester and cumulative GPA throughout your university career. Enter courses from each term to build a comprehensive academic record. Use the results for advising appointments, scholarship applications, and graduate school planning. No university login required.',
