      'title' => 'Nursing GPA Calculator - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free Nursing GPA Calculator to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Science GPA is a critical metric for professional school admissions, and our Nursing GPA Calculator helps you calculate nursing program prerequisite GPA accurately. Medical schools, dental schools, nursing programs, and other health professions require a separate science GPA (BCPM: Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Math) alongside your cumulative GPA. This science-specific GPA often carries more weight than your overall average.

AAMC (Association of American Medical Colleges) categorizes courses for science GPA calculation: Biology, Chemistry (including biochemistry), Physics, and Mathematics (including statistics). Only courses that fall into these four categories count toward your science GPA. A student with a 3.8 cumulative GPA but a 3.2 science GPA may find medical school admissions challenging because the science GPA reveals performance in the coursework most relevant to medical education.

Competitive medical school applicants typically have science GPAs of 3.5 or higher. For dental school, the average accepted student has a science GPA around 3.4. Nursing programs vary widely but often require 3.0+ in prerequisite science courses. Understanding your science GPA separately from your overall GPA helps you make informed decisions about whether to retake courses, pursue post-baccalaureate programs, or consider alternative career paths.

Enter only your science courses (biology, chemistry, physics, math) into our calculator to compute your science GPA. Compare this with your cumulative GPA to understand your competitive profile for professional school applications.',
