    'gpa-calculator-with-credits' => 
    array (
      'tool_slug' => 'gpa-calculator',
      'h1' => 'GPA Calculator with Credits',
      'title' => 'GPA Calculator with Credits - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free GPA Calculator with Credits to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Your Grade Point Average (GPA) is one of the most important numbers in your academic career. Our GPA Calculator with Credits makes credit-weighted GPA computation fast, accurate, and effortless. Whether you are a freshman tracking your first semester or a senior preparing graduation applications, this tool gives you instant results based on the standard 4.0 grading scale used by most American colleges and universities.

GPA is calculated by assigning a numerical value to each letter grade (A = 4.0, B = 3.0, C = 2.0, D = 1.0, F = 0.0), multiplying each grade value by the course credit hours, summing all quality points, and dividing by total credit hours. For example, if you earn an A (4.0) in a 3-credit course and a B (3.0) in a 4-credit course, your GPA is (12 + 12) / 7 = 3.43. This weighted average ensures that higher-credit courses have proportionally greater impact on your overall GPA.

Understanding your GPA is critical for scholarship eligibility, Dean\'s List recognition, graduate school admissions, and employment opportunities. Many programs require a minimum 3.0 GPA to maintain good academic standing, while competitive graduate programs often expect 3.5 or higher. Our calculator supports multiple semesters, allowing you to track your cumulative GPA across your entire academic career.

Our free tool requires no registration or downloads. Simply enter your courses, select letter grades, input credit hours, and get your GPA instantly. Add multiple semesters to see how each term affects your cumulative average. Use the related tools below to convert between GPA scales, calculate final grades, and estimate percentages.',
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How is GPA calculated?',
          'a' => 'GPA is calculated by multiplying each course grade point value by its credit hours, summing all quality points, and dividing by total credit hours. For example: (A x 3 credits + B x 4 credits) / 7 credits = GPA.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is a good GPA?',
          'a' => 'A good GPA depends on context. For college: 3.0+ is good, 3.5+ is very good, 3.7+ is excellent. For graduate school admissions, 3.3+ is typically expected.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is the highest GPA possible?',
          'a' => 'On the standard unweighted scale, 4.0 is the highest GPA (all As). On weighted scales that include AP/Honors courses, GPAs can exceed 4.0, up to 5.0.',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does GPA matter for getting a job?',
          'a' => 'Some employers screen for minimum GPA (often 3.0-3.5), especially for entry-level positions. After 2-3 years of work experience, GPA becomes less relevant.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can I raise my GPA after a bad semester?',
          'a' => 'Yes, but the more credits you have accumulated, the harder it is to change your cumulative GPA. Earning straight As in a 15-credit semester adds about 0.1 to your cumulative GPA.',
        ),
        5 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What GPA do I need for graduate school?',
          'a' => 'Most master programs expect 3.0+, competitive programs expect 3.3+, and top doctoral programs typically want 3.5+. Requirements vary by field and institution.',
        ),
      ),
      'instructions' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Enter your course name in the Course Name field (e.g., English 101, Calculus I).',
        1 => 'Select the letter grade you received for each course from the Grade dropdown.',
        2 => 'Enter the number of credit hours for each course in the Credits field.',
        3 => 'Click Add Course to add more courses to the current semester.',
        4 => 'Click Add Semester to track multiple terms for cumulative GPA.',
        5 => 'Your semester and cumulative GPA update automatically as you enter grades.',
      ),
