    'gpa-calculator-4-point-scale' => 
    array (
      'tool_slug' => 'gpa-calculator',
      'h1' => 'GPA Calculator 4 Point Scale',
      'title' => 'GPA Calculator 4 Point Scale - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free GPA Calculator 4 Point Scale to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'The unweighted GPA uses a standard 4.0 scale, and our GPA Calculator 4 Point Scale provides accurate 4-point GPA scale computation. Unlike weighted GPA, the unweighted scale treats all courses equally regardless of difficulty level. An A in AP Chemistry earns the same 4.0 as an A in regular English. This straightforward approach is preferred by many colleges for consistent cross-school comparisons.

The unweighted 4.0 scale assigns values as follows: A/A+ = 4.0, A- = 3.7, B+ = 3.3, B = 3.0, B- = 2.7, C+ = 2.3, C = 2.0, C- = 1.7, D+ = 1.3, D = 1.0, F = 0.0. Some schools use simplified scales without plus/minus distinctions. Our calculator supports the full scale with plus/minus grades for maximum accuracy.

Many colleges recalculate submitted GPAs on their own unweighted scale to normalize differences between high schools. The UC system, for example, calculates its own GPA using a specific formula that gives limited bonus points for AP and Honors courses. Understanding your unweighted GPA gives you the most conservative and universally comparable measure of academic performance.

Enter your courses, grade letters, and credit hours into our free tool to calculate your unweighted GPA instantly. No registration required. Track multiple semesters to see your academic trajectory and make informed decisions about your study habits and course planning.',
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is an unweighted GPA?',
          'a' => 'Unweighted GPA uses a standard 4.0 scale where A=4.0 regardless of course difficulty. This treats regular, Honors, and AP courses equally.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is unweighted GPA important for college?',
          'a' => 'Yes, many colleges recalculate all GPAs on an unweighted scale for fair comparison. It provides a standardized measure across different high schools.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is a good unweighted GPA for college?',
          'a' => 'State universities: 3.0+. Competitive schools: 3.5+. Elite universities: 3.8+. The national average is about 3.0 unweighted.',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I convert weighted to unweighted GPA?',
          'a' => 'Remove the bonus points from advanced courses. Recalculate using standard 4.0 values for all grades regardless of course level.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Does the 4.0 scale include plus/minus grades?',
          'a' => 'Yes, the full 4.0 scale includes A (4.0), A- (3.7), B+ (3.3), B (3.0), B- (2.7), C+ (2.3), C (2.0), C- (1.7), D+ (1.3), D (1.0), F (0.0).',
        ),
      ),
      'instructions' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Enter each course name without distinguishing difficulty level.',
        1 => 'Select the letter grade earned (A through F on the 4.0 scale).',
        2 => 'Input credit hours for each course.',
        3 => 'The calculator treats all courses equally on the standard 4.0 scale.',
        4 => 'Review your unweighted GPA, which is the standard measure most colleges use.',
        5 => 'Add all semesters for a complete unweighted cumulative GPA.',
      ),
      'related_slugs' => 
      array (
        0 => 'gpa-calculator',
        1 => 'college-gpa-calculator',
        2 => 'high-school-gpa-calculator',
        3 => 'cumulative-gpa-calculator',
        4 => 'weighted-gpa-calculator',
        5 => 'semester-gpa-calculator',
