      'h1' => 'GPA to Percentage Calculator',
      'title' => 'GPA to Percentage Calculator - Free Online Tool | ToolsHub',
      'meta_description' => 'Use our free GPA to Percentage Calculator to calculate your grade point average instantly. Supports weighted GPA, cumulative GPA, and semester GPA on the standard 4.0 scale.',
      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Converting between different grading systems is essential for academic planning, and our GPA to Percentage Calculator simplifies converting GPA to percentage. Whether you need to convert letter grades to GPA values, translate percentage scores to the 4.0 scale, or compare international grading systems, accurate conversion ensures you understand your academic standing.

The standard US conversion scale maps letter grades to GPA points: A+ = 4.0, A = 4.0, A- = 3.7, B+ = 3.3, B = 3.0, B- = 2.7, C+ = 2.3, C = 2.0, C- = 1.7, D+ = 1.3, D = 1.0, F = 0.0. For percentage-to-GPA conversion, common thresholds are: 93-100%% = 4.0 (A), 90-92%% = 3.7 (A-), 87-89%% = 3.3 (B+), 83-86%% = 3.0 (B), and so on. Note that conversion scales can vary by institution.

International students often need to convert their home-country grades to the US 4.0 scale. Indian percentage systems (typically 0-100), UK classification systems (First, 2:1, 2:2, Third), and European ECTS grades all require different conversion formulas. While no single conversion is universally accepted, our tool provides the standard US scale that most American colleges use as a baseline.

Enter your grades in letter format into our calculator and it will automatically apply the correct GPA point values. For percentage-based conversion, divide your grades into letter equivalents first, then use our calculator for the GPA computation. This gives you an accurate 4.0-scale GPA that you can compare across institutions.',
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I convert percentage to GPA?',
          'a' => 'Common conversion: 93-100%%=4.0, 90-92%%=3.7, 87-89%%=3.3, 83-86%%=3.0, 80-82%%=2.7, 77-79%%=2.3, 73-76%%=2.0, 70-72%%=1.7, 67-69%%=1.3, 60-66%%=1.0, below 60%%=0.0.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is an A- in GPA points?',
          'a' => 'An A- equals 3.7 grade points on the standard 4.0 scale used by most American colleges and universities.',
        ),
        2 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do I convert a 10-point GPA to 4.0?',
          'a' => 'Divide your grade on the 10-point scale by 10, then multiply by 4. For example, 8.5/10 x 4.0 = 3.40 approximate GPA.',
        ),
        3 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What GPA is a B+ average?',
          'a' => 'A B+ equals 3.3 on the 4.0 GPA scale. A pure B+ average across all courses would give you a 3.3 cumulative GPA.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'How do international grades convert to US GPA?',
          'a' => 'Conversion varies by country. Indian grading (60-100) roughly maps to 2.0-4.0. UK First Class approximates 3.7-4.0. Contact your target school for their accepted conversion.',
        ),
      ),
      'instructions' => 
      array (
        0 => 'Identify the grading system your scores are currently in (percentage, letter, etc.).',
        1 => 'Convert grades to the US letter grade equivalent using standard conversion tables.',
        2 => 'Enter the converted letter grades into the calculator.',
        3 => 'Input credit hours for each course (use 1 if credits do not apply).',
