      'default_options' => 
      array (
      ),
      'article' => 'Weather data drives every snow day decision, and our Snow Day Calculator AccuWeather leverages snow day prediction with AccuWeather data to deliver reliable predictions. Professional weather services like AccuWeather, the National Weather Service, and local meteorologists provide the snowfall forecasts, winter storm warnings, and ice advisories that school administrators use when making closure decisions.

The connection between weather forecasts and school closures is direct: when the National Weather Service issues a Winter Storm Warning (6+ inches expected) or an Ice Storm Warning, schools in affected areas cancel classes roughly 80-90%% of the time. Winter Weather Advisories (2-4 inches) trigger closures about 40-60%% of the time, depending on the district\'s location and infrastructure. Our calculator incorporates these weather-to-closure correlations.

Modern weather prediction has improved dramatically thanks to satellite imagery, Doppler radar networks, and advanced atmospheric modeling. However, winter storms remain among the hardest weather events to forecast precisely because small temperature differences at the surface determine whether precipitation falls as rain, sleet, freezing rain, or snow. A storm predicted to drop 6 inches of snow could instead produce 2 inches of ice, which is actually more dangerous for transportation.

Our snow day calculator helps you interpret weather forecasts into actionable school closure predictions. Enter the forecasted snow amount, select conditions like ice and extreme wind, choose your region type, and get an instant probability estimate that reflects real-world closure patterns.',
