      'article' => '## Staying Complying with IRS Guidelines

Our **IRS Tax Withholding Calculator (Estimate Your Paycheck Tax)** was built from the ground up to align with modern IRS Pub 15 and Pub 15-T guidelines. Ensuring your withholding is correct is critical for financial health and avoiding year-end surprises.

### IRS Trust Signals in 2026

- **Form W-4 Accuracy**: The IRS redesigned the W-4 to eliminate \'exemptions\' in favor of a simpler dollar-based system.
- **Tax Estimation**: The IRS recommends checking your withholding at least twice a year—especially if you have a life event like marriage or a new child.
- **Safe Harbor Rules**: Generally, if you pay at least 90% of your current year tax or 100% of your prior year tax, you avoid underpayment penalties.

### Using the IRS-Style Approach

