          array (
            'q' => 'Why is there no exact formula for ellipse circumference?',
            'a' => 'The circumference involves an "elliptic integral," which cannot be expressed using simple arithmetic or basic math functions. Therefore, we use high-precision approximations.',
          ),
          1 => 
          array (
            'q' => 'What are a and b in an ellipse?',
            'a' => 'The major axis is the total width, and the minor axis is the total height. "a" and "b" are the semi-axes, meaning they are half of those total lengths.',
          ),
          2 => 
          array (
            'q' => 'How accurate is this calculator?',
            'a' => 'We use Ramanujan\'s formula, which is accurate to within a tiny fraction of a percent for almost all real-world ellipses.',
