            'q' => 'What is the Euler formula?',
            'a' => 'The formula is V - E + F = 2, where V is Vertices, E is Edges, and F is Faces. It applies to all convex polyhedra.',
          ),
          1 => 
          array (
            'q' => 'What counts as a vertex?',
            'a' => 'A vertex is any "corner" point where two or more edges meet on a 3D shape.',
          ),
          2 => 
          array (
            'q' => 'Does this work for a sphere?',
            'a' => 'Yes, topologically, a convex polyhedron is equivalent to a sphere, which is why the characteristic is 2.',
          ),
          3 => 
