        'meta_description' => 'Solve any triangle by entering three known values. Calculates all angles, sides, area, and perimeter using Law of Sines and Cosines.',
        'article' => 'Solving a triangle means finding all its unknown side lengths and angles. For a standard triangle, there are six properties in total (three sides and three angles). If you know at least three of these properties (with at least one being a side length), you can find the remaining three using trigonometry. Our General Triangle Solver is designed to handle this complex task with ease, supporting all the common cases taught in geometry and used in professional fields like surveying and navigation.

The two main "weapons" of a triangle solver are the Law of Sines and the Law of Cosines. The Law of Sines ($a/\\sin A = b/\\sin B = c/\\sin C$) is perfect for cases like Angle-Side-Angle (ASA) or Angle-Angle-Side (AAS). The Law of Cosines ($c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab \\cos C$) is used when you know all three sides (SSS) or two sides and the included angle (SAS). Our tool automatically selects the correct method based on the data you provide.

One of the unique challenges in triangle solving is the "Ambigous Case" (SSA), where knowing two sides and a non-included angle can result in zero, one, or two possible triangles. Our solver detects these situations and provides all valid solutions, ensuring you have the complete geometric picture. In addition to the missing parts, the calculator also computes the Area (using Heron\'s formula for sides or trigonometric formulas for angles), the Perimeter, and even the altitudes of the triangle.

Whether you are designing a roof truss, calculating the path of a ship, or finishing a math assignment, this tool provides instant, accurate results. It eliminates the need for manual table lookups and tedious multi-step calculations, giving you more time to focus on your design or analysis. The solver supports both degree and radian modes to match your specific requirements.',
