        'article' => 'The Golden Section is a way of dividing a line or a quantity into two unequal parts such that the ratio of the whole to the larger part is the same as the ratio of the larger part to the smaller part. This ratio is known as the Golden Ratio, or Phi ($\\phi$), and is approximately 1.618. Our Golden Section Calculator is a precise tool for anyone looking to apply these divine proportions to their work, from financial analysis to creative projects.

