The Golden Section is deeply connected to the Fibonacci Sequence. As you progress further in the sequence (1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13...), the ratio between consecutive numbers gets closer and closer to Phi. This connection explains why the ratio appears so often in nature—in the arrangement of leaves on a stem, the scales of a pinecone, and the geometry of seeds in a sunflower.

