        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What does a Current Ratio of exactly 1.0 mean?',
          'a' => 'It means perfectly balanced working capital. For every dollar owed in the next year, the company holds exactly one dollar in short-term assets to pay for it. However, it leaves zero margin for error if receivables default or inventory expires.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Why is it also called the Working Capital ratio?',
          'a' => 'Because Working Capital is calculated as (Current Assets - Current Liabilities). The Current Ratio just expresses this identical relationship as a quotient rather than a raw dollar amount.',
