          'q' => 'Can IV predict the exact direction of the stock price?',
          'a' => 'No. Implied volatility is strictly non-directional. A high IV simply indicates that the market expects a massive explosive move—but the options market does not explicitly denote whether that explosion will be a parabolic move to the upside or a catastrophic crash to the downside.',
        ),
