          'q' => 'Why did I get liquidated before my account hit exactly zero?',
          'a' => 'Exchanges will never allow your account balance to slip into the negative, as this puts the broker’s own funds at risk. They liquidate you early based on the maintenance margin rule. The leftover fraction of a percentage pays for exchange liquidation fees and slippage protection.',
        ),
        4 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Can borrowing fees (funding rates) change my liquidation price?',
          'a' => 'Yes. In perpetual futures markets and heavily margined stock accounts, borrowing money incurs daily or hourly fees. These continuous, silent deductions are taken directly from your margin equity. As your equity shrinks due to fee bleed, your liquidation target slowly inches closer to the current price.',
